sections.text:
spokenform.prepare() applies explicit stages in this order:


validate the selected language and protected ranges;


discover caller-protected ranges and auto-detected literals such as URLs,
email addresses, and (when not claimed semantically) semantic versions;
normalize_literals=True opts high-confidence URL, e-mail, version, and
contextual Roman rendering into structured ownership while caller spans
remain absolute;


obtain or validate optional lexical annotations;


replace protected ranges with internal sentinels and remap annotation offsets;


normalize Unicode independently when enabled;


recognize complete high-confidence structured sequences, then ask abbr2words
for source-aligned structured quantity identities and realize them with the
selected locale’s semantic grammar;


exp…

